-- title:
--   Unique homomorphic extension of a semilinear S-action to a constant-field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $F$, $K'$, $F'$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, $F'$ a $K'$-algebra, $K'$ a $K$-algebra, $F'$ an $F$-algebra and a $K$-algebra, the two towers $K \to K' \to F'$ and $K \to F \to F'$ being compatible, and assume $K$ is algebraically closed of characteristic zero. Assume further: $F$ contains an element $x$ transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over $K(x)$, and likewise $F'$ contains an element transcendental over $K'$ over whose $K'$-adjunction $F'$ is finite-dimensional; and the $K'$-subfield of $F'$ generated by the image of $F$ is all of $F'$. Let $S$ be a group, $\mathrm{galF} : S \to \mathrm{SemilinearAut}\,K\,F$ a monoid homomorphism into the group of pairs $(\varphi,\psi)$ with $\varphi$ a ring automorphism of $F$, $\psi$ one of $K$, and $\varphi \circ \mathrm{algebraMap} = \mathrm{algebraMap} \circ \psi$, and $\tau : S \to (K' \simeq_{+*} K')$ a monoid homomorphism such that for all $\sigma$ the automorphism $\tau(\sigma)$ restricted along $K \to K'$ agrees with the $K$-component $\mathrm{baseAut}(\mathrm{galF}(\sigma))$. Then there is a unique monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{galF}' : S \to \mathrm{SemilinearAut}\,K'\,F'$ whose $K'$-component at each $\sigma$ is $\tau(\sigma)$ and whose action on $F'$ satisfies $\mathrm{galF}'(\sigma)\cdot \mathrm{algebraMap}_{F}^{F'}(y) = \mathrm{algebraMap}_{F}^{F'}(\mathrm{galF}(\sigma)\cdot y)$ for all $\sigma \in S$, $y \in F$.
--
--   This is the group-equivariant form of the statement that a semilinear automorphism of a one-variable function field over an algebraically closed constant field extends uniquely along a constant-field extension: an action of $S$ on $F$ by semilinear automorphisms, compatible over $K$ with a given action on $K'$, extends uniquely to a semilinear action on $F' = F\cdot K'$. It is used in the construction of a Shimura curve model with good reduction together with an equivariant uniformisation in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_SemilinearAut_existsUnique_monoidHom_baseAut_eq_smul_algebraMap_eq_of_constantFieldExtension.lean

